abstract: >
  Hardware–Software Co-Evolution of Intelligence (HSCI) proposes that
  intelligence does not necessarily begin with complete internal
  representation. Physical and sensory differences may already become
  intelligence-relevant when they create structural consequences such as
  salience, triggering, routing, state change, control activation, or action.
  The framework develops Intelligence Before Representation, the Structural
  Consequence Boundary, Hardware and Pre-Representational Intelligence
  Primitives, Hardware Function Tunnels, Per-Function Intelligence Placement,
  Selective Upward Escalation, Downward Structural Consolidation, and
  multi-substrate Brain-Unit AI. Autonomous drones are proposed as a canonical
  engineering testbed for measuring the trade-offs among energy, latency,
  computation, representation cost, reliability, and safety.

