  abstract: >
    Hardware–Software Co-Evolution of Intelligence (HSCI) develops a
    multi-substrate view of intelligence in which physical selectivity,
    resonance, salience, structural triggering, Function Tunnels, neural
    computation, world models, and generative reasoning can cooperate across
    different layers and timescales. Its foundational hypothesis is that
    intelligence may begin before general representation when a physical or
    sensory difference acquires structural consequence.

